---
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import MeetingJoinDetails from '../components/MeetingJoinDetails.astro';
import { VermontTime } from '../domain/VermontTime.ts';
import { AstroContent } from '../persistence/AstroContent.ts';

const committee = await AstroContent.loadCommittee();
const now = VermontTime.now();
const nextMeeting = committee.nextMeeting({ now });
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Home"
  description="Burlington, South Burlington, and Winooski are studying whether to merge under Vermont's Act 170. A study is required. A merger is not."
  updatedOn={committee.updatedOn()}
>
  <h1>Should our three school districts become one?</h1>
  <p class="lede">A study is required. A merger is not.</p>
  <p>
    Under Vermont's <a href="/act-170/">Act 170 (2026)</a>, school districts across the state must study possible
    mergers. Burlington, South Burlington, and Winooski are studying this question together. A committee of school
    board members from all three districts is doing the study. The committee has not decided anything.
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="next-meeting">
    <div class="panel">
      <h2 id="next-meeting">Next meeting</h2>
      {
        nextMeeting ? (
          <>
            <MeetingJoinDetails meeting={nextMeeting} now={now} />
            {nextMeeting.hasPostedAgenda() && (
              <p>
                <a href={`${nextMeeting.path()}#agenda`}>Read the agenda</a>
              </p>
            )}
            <p>
              <a class="button" href={nextMeeting.path()}>
                Meeting details
              </a>{' '}
              <a class="button" href={nextMeeting.calendarFilePath()}>
                Add to calendar
              </a>
            </p>
          </>
        ) : (
          <p>No meeting is scheduled yet. See <a href="/meetings/">past meetings</a>.</p>
        )
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="local-decision">
    <h2 id="local-decision">Required process, local decision</h2>
    <p>
      The state requires the study, but it does not decide the outcome. If the committee recommends a merger, voters in
      each community decide whether to approve it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each school board chose representatives for the committee. A regional facilitator, {committee.facilitator.name},
      guides the committee's work. <a href="/members/">Meet the committee members</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="questions">
    <h2 id="questions">The four questions we must answer together</h2>
    <h3>Educational opportunity</h3>
    <p>
      How would a merger affect course variety, access to career and technical education (CTE), and middle and high
      school programs?
    </p>
    <h3>Governance</h3>
    <p>What would a combined school board look like? How would each community be represented?</p>
    <h3>Money and operations</h3>
    <p>
      How would a merger affect taxes, spending, buildings, and each district's ability to handle budget pressure?
    </p>
    <h3>Long-term sustainability</h3>
    <p>Would merging be sustainable, both financially and for students? What are the risks of staying separate?</p>
    <p>
      The committee must also report what is working well in each district today. If members disagree, the report must
      include the views of those who disagree.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="what-comes-next">
    <h2 id="what-comes-next">Where we are and what comes next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>October 20, 2026:</strong> The committee held its first meeting.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>First Monday of each month, 4:00 p.m. Eastern Time:</strong> The committee meets in locations rotating
        between the three districts. Anyone may attend.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>By September 1, 2027:</strong> The committee shares its final report. If it recommends a merger, it also
        shares a proposed plan for the new district, called the "articles of agreement."
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>By December 1, 2027:</strong> The Secretary of Education reviews any proposed merger and makes a
        recommendation to the State Board of Education.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>By December 15, 2027:</strong> The State Board of Education issues its findings.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>March 7, 2028 (Town Meeting Day):</strong> If a merger is recommended, voters in each district vote on
        it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>July 1, 2029:</strong> If voters approve, the new district would begin for the 2029 to 2030 school year.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="necessary-and-advisable">
    <h2 id="necessary-and-advisable">What "necessary" and "advisable" mean</h2>
    <p>
      If the committee recommends a merger, it will label each district one of two ways. A necessary district must vote
      yes for the merger to happen. An advisable district joins only if its own voters say yes. The merger can go ahead
      without an advisable district.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="feedback">
    <h2 id="feedback">Have questions or feedback?</h2>
    <p>
      Come to a committee meeting in person, by video, or by phone. Every meeting has time for public comment, and you
      can send a written comment to be read aloud. <a href="/participate/">How to participate</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each school board is also gathering input from its own community. Visit your district's website to learn more:{' '}
      {
        committee.districts.map((district, index) => (
          <>
            <a href={district.act170Page ?? district.website}>{district.city}</a>
            {index === committee.districts.length - 1 ? '.' : index === committee.districts.length - 2 ? ', and ' : ', '}
          </>
        ))
      }
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
